  "notes": "From English 'chat.' Refers specifically to text-based real-time communication via apps or the internet, not face-to-face chatting.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- チャットする: to chat (online)\n- チャットで{話|はな}す: to talk via chat\n- グループチャット: group chat\n- ビデオチャット: video chat\n- チャットアプリ: chat app\n- チャットルーム: chat room\n\nUSAGE IN JAPAN:\nLINE is the dominant messaging app in Japan, so {日本語|にほんご} speakers often say LINEする (to LINE someone) rather than チャットする in daily conversation. チャット is used more broadly or when not referring to a specific app.\n\nREGISTER:\nNeutral to casual. Widely understood across all age groups.",
